een we've been working with  uh international partners who have put a  similar  uh package in place new zealand  australia for example to see how that  works  it's very easy for you to say oh all you  have to do is  but uh hindsight is is a wonderful thing  and actually  um as i say this is this is adding to  an existing package of measures which  requires  a uh a test before uh departure  requires a notification form upon  departure  already requires 10 days of quarantine  so this is adding to existing measures  and we want to make sure that this works  that we give the hotel industry  notice obviously not every hotel will be  doing this and so it's unsurprising that  some hotel chains haven't been  contacted about this but the uh the the  package we're putting together uh this  quarantine package adds to an existing  suite of measures  to protect ourselves at the border you  say we're talking to  to our counterparts like australia and  new zealand um  the health minister didn't talk to  australia his australian counterpart  until yesterday  still hasn't spoken as far as we're  aware to new zealand about it i mean  they've been doing this  for months surely they've got a template  wouldn't the first thing to do would be  on the first date to phone new zealand  phone australia  how have you done it what's the template  let's get it underway in a few days  well as i say we are we are uh working  with international partners  on this as we have slowly and actually  and actually  the um the uk has been  uh the uk has been coordinating our  response to coronavirus internationally  just as  all countries have done but i think it's  you know i i'll reinforce the point that  this is adding to  an existing suite of measures  that already sees a requirement for  testing before arrival  quarantine on arrival this is  strengthening an already strong set of  border measures and and  and it needs to be seen in that context  okay um  let's get back to that red list one and  a half